…and currentTime() itself appends the row:
        ctx.setReplaying(false);
        var now = Instant.now();
        appendEvent(ctx, seq, EventType.SIDE_EFFECT, "$maestro:currentTime", serializer.serialize(now));
        return now;

So a TIMED awaitSignal records a $maestro:currentTime SIDE_EFFECT to make its deadline
replay-deterministic. The loan workflow's two withdrawal gates are timed awaits, which is
why the rows sit at 6/7 (before the document + withdrawn awaits at 8/9) and 13/14 (before
the package.signed + withdrawn awaits at 15/16).

IMPACT: §D5 tells the presenter, verbatim, 'There is no SIDE_EFFECT row to point at'.
The FIRST event log the demo puts on screen (§1) contains four of them, and §D2 invites the
room to read that very table. A questioner reading the screen contradicts the presenter.
The engine-behaviour explanation is better material than the disclaimer it replaces.
